## UI

420px Automation edit dialog using the provider-backed configuration controls and local asynchronous Save lifecycle. This screenshot is from the earlier Copilot pass; the latest live verification also covered Codex as described above.

![Automation dialog at 420px](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d167b0d-8f5c-40ce-b9e8-0773f2f11ef7)

Clicking a file in the current-turn changes list and then clicking anywhere else left the row rendered with the blue focus outline and active-selection background.

The chat transcript is itself a `monaco-list`, and `DefaultStyleController` emits focus/selection styles as **descendant** selectors:

```ts
// src/vs/base/browser/ui/list/listWidget.ts
content.push(`.monaco-list${suffix}:focus .monaco-list-row.focused { background-color: ${styles.listFocusBackground}; }`);
content.push(`.monaco-list${suffix}:focus .monaco-list-row.selected { background-color: ${styles.listActiveSelectionBackground}; }`);
```

`suffix` scopes the rule to one list *container*, but the row half is a plain descendant match — so rows of the nested changed-files list pick up the transcript's active styling as soon as the transcript takes DOM focus. Rows open with `preserveFocus: true`, so the nested row stays focused until the next click elsewhere, which is exactly when the leak becomes visible.

## Description

- **`chatChangesSummaryPart.ts`** — `renderChangesSummaryFileList` now drops the list's focus and selection once DOM focus moves out, mirroring `notificationsList.ts`. This is the shared helper, so both the current-turn changes pill and the checkpoint changes summary are covered.

  ```ts
  const focusTracker = store.add(dom.trackFocus(listNode));
  store.add(focusTracker.onDidBlur(() => {
      if (!dom.isAncestorOfActiveElement(listNode)) {
          list.setFocus([]);
          list.setSelection([]);
      }
  }));
  ```

  The guard is `isAncestorOfActiveElement` rather than `document.hasFocus()`: a deactivated window keeps its `activeElement`, so the row state survives an app switch, while a real focus move inside the document clears it. `hasFocus()` additionally reports `false` in the hidden unit-test window, making that variant untestable.

- **`chatChangesSummaryPart.test.ts`** — regression test that clicks a row, moves focus to a sibling element, and asserts the row drops both classes. Hidden test windows update `document.activeElement` without dispatching focus events, so the test announces the moves to the tracker via synthetic `focusin`/`focusout`; it fails without the production change in both the browser and Electron runners.

Note: `setSelection([])` passes no `browserEvent`, and `ResourceNavigator` only opens on keyboard-originated selection changes, so this does not trigger a spurious editor open.

