fixes https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-internalbacklog/issues/8830

## Description

Sessions could report `inProgress` forever when the Copilot CLI runtime went away while a turn was running — the chat spins until the user sends another message, which cancels the prior turn and restarts reasoning.

A turn is driven entirely by SDK notifications: `session.send` resolves as soon as the runtime accepts the prompt, so from then on there is no outstanding request that a dying connection could reject. `CopilotAgent._recoverFromClosedConnection` — which already fails active turns with a retryable `providerConnectionClosed` error and drops the dead client — is only reachable from a *failing operation*, so a runtime that dies mid-turn is never noticed and the turn is never completed, cancelled or errored.

### Changes

- **`copilotAgent.ts`**: added `_updateTurnKeepalive()` / `_runTurnKeepaliveProbe()` — a `client.ping()` liveness probe armed only while at least one chat has an in-flight turn (30s interval, one probe at a time). A closed-connection rejection is routed into the existing recovery path, so stranded turns get a terminal, retryable error. Armed after `sendMessage`, re-evaluated on turn end, cleared on client stop/shutdown, so it costs nothing while idle.
- **`copilotFailureTelemetry.ts`**: added `'keepalive'` to `CopilotClientFailureOperation` so these failures are distinguishable from operation-detected ones.
- **`copilotAgent.test.ts`**: `TestCopilotClient` gained a `ping()` stub (with an injectable `pingError`) plus a fast `_turnKeepaliveIntervalMs` override on `TestableCopilotAgent`; two tests cover recovery on a dead connection mid-turn and the idle no-probe case.

```ts
private async _runTurnKeepaliveProbe(): Promise<void> {
    const client = this._client;
    if (this._shutdownPromise || !client || this._chatsWithActiveTurn() === 0) {
        return;
    }
    this._turnKeepaliveProbeRunning = true;
    try {
        await client.ping();
    } catch (error) {
        // Only a closed connection is actionable: any other rejection
        // leaves the runtime able to keep driving the turn.
        await this._recoverFromClosedConnection(error, 'keepalive').catch(/* ... */);
    } finally {
        this._turnKeepaliveProbeRunning = false;
        this._updateTurnKeepalive();
    }
}
```

Note this is the client-side half. The CLI-side fixes suggested in the issue (turn-aware shutdown, always writing a terminal `turn_end`, a non-`routine` shutdown type) still belong in the runtime; the probe makes VS Code deterministic regardless of which component kills the connection.

